```java
@Configuration // CGLIB-proxied; @Bean methods are honored
class AppConfig {
    @Bean // Spring calls this once and stores the result
    ObjectMapper objectMapper() {
        var mapper = new ObjectMapper();
        mapper.registerModule(new JavaTimeModule()); // configure it
        return mapper; // becomes the "objectMapper" bean
    }
}
```
Moving the method into a `@Configuration` class is what turns it into a real bean factory.

